      "version": 1236,
      "versionNonce": 1447884635,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1765810965312,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "~ AI  Features \n1. When fetching a link, currently my back-end only \n    fetches the raw link and displays title & description \n    when it's available, so I am thinking on adding an AI\n    Agent, which can somehow fetch the correct description\n    and title, so it'll do 2 things, adds a good UX & also adds\n    a layer of AI, makes my app robust, the main thing is adding \n    robustness to my application, so user's do not get a \n    a simple app name as the title \n\n\n~ Security Feature \n1. Study about the XSS attacks and also implement a basic level \n    of security in my application as users can save random links  \n    and also application has to have some kinda security, so the \n    security part in non-negotiable\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "~ AI  Features \n1. When fetching a link, currently my back-end only \n    fetches the raw link and displays title & description \n    when it's available, so I am thinking on adding an AI\n    Agent, which can somehow fetch the correct description\n    and title, so it'll do 2 things, adds a good UX & also adds\n    a layer of AI, makes my app robust, the main thing is adding \n    robustness to my application, so user's do not get a \n    a simple app name as the title \n\n\n~ Security Feature \n1. Study about the XSS attacks and also implement a basic level \n    of security in my application as users can save random links  \n    and also application has to have some kinda security, so the \n    security part in non-negotiable\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
